training_program:
  name: "English-Based Contribution Publishing Training"
  slug: "english-based-contribution-publishing"
  priority: 2
  status: active
  start_date: 2026-06-01
  end_date: 2026-06-28
  duration: 4 weeks
  purpose: |
    Build confidence through small, successful experiences of expressing work
    context, questions, insights, and progress in English.
    Problem: thoughts, questions, and insights often stay internal due to hesitation,
    low confidence, or fear of judgment.
    Behavior change: move from silent understanding to visible contribution —
    externalizing work context and user impact in short, clear English.
  daily_actions:
    - Write one work-related English sentence (internal practice)
    - Draft one English question or sharing message related to current work
    - Add English impact or verification note to a PR, Jira, RFC, or document when relevant
    - Send a question or status update via Slack/DM when there is a clear and useful message
    - Use a prepared English sentence in a 1:1 when possible
    - Ask a short clarification question or share one opinion in a team meeting when appropriate
  daily_score:
    name: Contribution Publishing Score
    note: |
      Measures psychological difficulty of communication actions and degree of
      externalization. Not a measure of perfect English.
      Count repeated actions if meaningfully separate.
      If same content is copied to multiple places, count only the highest-difficulty action.
      If a draft was meaningfully improved before sharing, the draft can also be counted.
      Do not judge grammar. Evaluate whether work context and intention were communicated.
    criteria:
      - "Write one work-related English sentence alone: 1 point"
      - "Draft an English question or sharing message: 2 points"
      - "Add English impact/verification to PR/Jira/RFC/document: 3 points"
      - "Send a question or status update via Slack/DM: 4 points"
      - "Use a prepared English sentence in a 1:1: 5 points"
      - "Ask a question or share an opinion in a team meeting: 6 points"
  daily_reflection:
    style: lightweight, AI-assisted, max 3 questions
    questions:
      - What work-related thought, question, or update did you try to express in English today?
      - Where did you externalize it? (alone / draft / PR/Jira/RFC/doc / Slack/DM / 1:1 / meeting)
      - What do you want to express tomorrow, and what is the smallest realistic way to do it?
    ai_output_after_answers:
      - Summarize what was externalized today
      - Calculate the Contribution Publishing Score
      - Identify externalization level (Level 1–4)
      - Evaluate one representative message using English Contribution Quality Score (out of 5)
      - Point out one thing done well
      - Point out one missing or avoided part (without blame)
      - Suggest realistic actions for tomorrow by difficulty
      - Improve the user's English sentence into a short, natural version
      - Ask which action the user will choose for tomorrow (optional)
  english_contribution_quality_score:
    scale: 5
    criteria:
      - "Context: Is it clear which ticket, work, or situation this is about?"
      - "My understanding: Does it show how I currently understand the situation?"
      - "User/product/work impact: Does it show why this matters?"
      - "Clear question/request: Is it clear what I want the other person to do?"
      - "Next action: Would the answer change what I do next?"
  weekly_reflection:
    style: user-led, ~30 minutes, AI guides with questions one at a time
    focus:
      - actual experience
      - friction and avoidance
      - effectiveness and visibility
      - system adjustment
    structure:
      - Fact review (days practiced, actions done, externalization levels)
      - Experience review (most meaningful moment, most uncomfortable moment)
      - Score vs actual growth (did score reflect real growth? scoring adjustments?)
      - Avoidance analysis (what was avoided and why? what is the smaller version?)
      - Next week experiment (keep/reduce/try harder/minimum goal/challenge goal/one-sentence rule)
    final_output:
      - What actually happened this week
      - Most meaningful moment
      - Most uncomfortable moment
      - Training effect
      - Scoring system adjustment
      - Keep / reduce / try harder next week
      - Minimum goal and challenge goal for next week
      - One-sentence rule for next week
  reminders:
    daily:
      time: "21:00 CET"
      message: "Reflect on today's English contribution. What did you try to express today?"
    weekly:
      day_time: "Saturday 21:00 CET"
      message: "Do your weekly English contribution review."
  review_rules:
    adjust_if: |
      Daily reflection feels too heavy, actions are avoided because they are too big,
      score does not reflect actual psychological difficulty,
      or actions are not connected to real work.
    pause_if: |
      No realistic work context for English communication for several days,
      or the training creates more guilt than useful feedback.
    complete_if: |
      Can consistently write or say short English work updates/questions,
      can use prepared sentences in 1:1 or Slack/DM without excessive hesitation,
      can occasionally speak up in team meetings with short questions or opinions.
